//BUG="FEEDBACK.md 1.5 — a file with no code panics the preprocessor"
//ERR any
//MSG="No main function found"

// parse_indentation seeds `lines` with one empty entry and then retains away
// every blank line (src/compiler/preprocessor.rs); when nothing is left,
// parse_indentation_block still reads lines[0] and panics with
// "index out of bounds: the len is 0 but the index is 0". This file is exactly
// that case — every line in it is a comment.
//
// The right behaviour is the ordinary "No main function found" error. While
// fixing it, note that display_error's `lines.len() - 1` underflows on a
// source with no lines (FEEDBACK.md 1.16), which this bug currently hides.
